.TH FL-SYSINFO 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-sysinfo \- system information
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-sysinfo\fR [\fB\-\-page\fR \fIPAGE\fR] [\fB\-\-report\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows what the computer is made of and how it is doing, read from \fI/proc\fR, \fI/sys\fR and
\fI/etc/os-release\fR (no administrator rights needed). The pages:
.TP
\fBOverview\fR (overview)
The computer's model, the operating system, kernel, desktop and session, how long it has been
running, a summary of the hardware, and the firmware (BIOS or UEFI, mainboard).
.TP
\fBProcessor\fR (processor)
Name, vendor, sockets, cores and threads, virtualization, the speed range and the current speed of
every CPU, the frequency governor, the caches and the state of the CPU vulnerability mitigations.
.TP
\fBMemory\fR (memory)
Memory in use and available, swap (also zram) and huge pages.
.TP
\fBGraphics\fR (graphics)
Graphics cards with their driver, PCI slot and video memory, and the state and mode of every output.
.TP
\fBStorage\fR (storage)
Disks (kind, size, serial number, firmware) and the mounted file systems with their free space.
.TP
\fBNetwork\fR (network)
Network interfaces: kind, state, speed, hardware address, driver and IP addresses.
.TP
\fBDevices\fR (devices)
PCI and USB devices (named from the \fIpci.ids\fR and \fIusb.ids\fR databases of hwdata when
installed), input devices and sound cards.
.TP
\fBPower & Sensors\fR (power)
Batteries (charge, health, charge cycles), the power supply, and temperatures and fan speeds;
read again every 2 seconds while the page is shown.
.PP
Select a row and press Ctrl+C (or right-click it) to copy it; a heading copies its group.
\fBCopy All\fR copies the whole report, \fBSave Report\fR (Ctrl+S) saves it as a text file.
F5 reads the page again, Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+8 go to a page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-page\fR \fIPAGE\fR
Opens that page (the names in parentheses above).
.TP
\fB\-\-report\fR
Prints the whole report as text and quits.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-taskmgr\fR(1), \fBfl-settings\fR(1)
